## 1️⃣ Top‑Rated Activities (All within walking distance)

| Rank | Attraction | Why It’s a Must‑Do | Approx. Cost (per adult) | Notes |
|------|------------|--------------------|--------------------------|-------|
| 1 | **Royal BC Museum** | World‑class natural history & First Nations exhibits; “Living History” brings 19th‑century Victoria to life. | **$30** | Open 10 am‑5 pm (Mon‑Sat). |
| 2 | **Inner Harbour & Parliament Buildings** | Iconic waterfront, daily flag‑raising, and the stunning Parliament. | **Free** (optional guided tour $15) | Best in the morning or late afternoon. |
| 3 | **Craigdarroch Castle** | Victorian‑era mansion with exquisite stained‑glass, woodwork, and a ghost‑story. | **$20** | Open 10 am‑5 pm (Mon‑Sat). |

> **Pro tip:** All three are within a 15‑minute walk of each other, so you can easily combine them into a single day.

---

## 2️⃣ Highly‑Reviewed Hotels (3‑room block)

| Rank | Hotel | Room Type | Price (per night, 3 rooms) | Highlights |
|------|-------|-----------|----------------------------|------------|
| 1 | **Fairmont Empress** | 3‑bedroom suite (or 3 single rooms) | **$1,200** | Historic luxury, ocean view, on‑site spa. |
| 2 | **Hotel Grand Pacific** | 3‑bedroom suite (or 3 single rooms) | **$1,050** | Rooftop bar, close to Inner Harbour. |
| 3 | **The Oakes Hotel** | 3‑bedroom suite (or 3 single rooms) | **$950** | Boutique vibe, garden terrace, free breakfast. |

> **Booking note:** All three hotels offer a “family” or “group” rate for multiple rooms. Book directly through the hotel’s website or a trusted travel portal to lock in the best rate and confirm the 3‑room block.

---

## 3️⃣ Sample Itinerary

| Day | Morning | Afternoon | Evening |
|-----|---------|-----------|---------|
| **Nov 15** | Arrive & check‑in | Explore Inner Harbour & Parliament | Dinner at a waterfront restaurant |
| **Nov 16** | Royal BC Museum | Lunch in Chinatown | Sunset cruise (optional) |
| **Nov 17** | Craigdarroch Castle | Shopping on Government Street | Nightlife or a quiet walk |
| **Nov 18** | Check‑out | Last‑minute souvenir shopping | Depart |

---

### Quick Checklist

- **Flights/Ferry:** Confirm arrival time to Victoria International Airport (YVR) or ferry if coming from Vancouver.  
- **Reservations:** Book the 3‑room block by **Oct 31** to secure the best rate.  
- **Tickets:** Pre‑purchase tickets for the Royal BC Museum and Craigdarroch Castle to skip the lines.  
- **Packing:** November in Victoria is cool & rainy—layers, waterproof jacket, comfortable walking shoes.

Enjoy your adventure in Victoria! If you’d like help with booking links, travel insurance, or anything else, just let me know.

